                    <note type="editorial">  See <title>DNB</title>.
     <p>Godwin records his death. There are four more possible
     appearances - two meetings in 1793 (one at the theatre with Robinson, one at Robinson's) and
     two letters written by Godwin in 1802.  These are likely to be Arthur
     Murphy.   Murphy edited  <title>The Works of Cornelius Tacitus, with an Essay on the Life and Genius of Tacitus</title>, in 4 vols. which was published by Robinson in 1793.</p></note>
                    <bibl type="printedbook"> Arthur Murphy, ed., <title>The Works of Cornelius Tacitus, with an 
